{"case_id": "case:38b61c5a333e9c64fac8", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "All twelve k1 codes are distinct (u01 through u12), so no first-collection source item contributes more than one `a` measurement to the procedure.", "observed_value": ["u01","u02","u03","u04","u05","u06","u07","u08","u09","u10","u11","u12"], "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0"}]}, {"description": "All twelve k2 codes are distinct (v01,v03,...,v23), so no second-collection source item contributes more than one `b` measurement.", "observed_value": ["v07","v09","v11","v13","v15","v17","v19","v21","v23","v01","v03","v05"], "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0"}]}, {"description": "The procedure applied is an independent two-sample t-test over all rows; with one row per unit on each side this row-independent procedure receives exactly one entry per unit.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.ttest_ind(left, right)"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "df=np.float64(22.0)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The closest candidate evidence for the issue class would be a duplicated k1 or k2 code feeding multiple rows into ttest_ind; I searched both key columns and found no repeated code, so no repeated-unit entry is demonstrated.", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "k1,k2,tag,a,b"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict by enumerating every k1 and every k2 value across all 12 data rows looking for any repetition, and by checking whether the reported df (22 = 12+12-2) implied more entries than distinct units. Both checks failed to produce a repeated unit: 12 distinct k1 codes map to 12 `a` entries and 12 distinct k2 codes map to 12 `b` entries, one each.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"},
{"case_id": "case:52e3f52739576660f136", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "All 24 k1 codes are distinct (u01 through u24, in shuffled order), so each first-collection unit contributes exactly one `a` entry.", "observed_value": ["u07","u08","u09","u10","u11","u12","u01","u02","u03","u06","u05","u04","u19","u20","u21","u22","u23","u24","u13","u14","u15","u18","u17","u16"], "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "u07,v12,t01,1.0,2.0"}]}, {"description": "All 24 k2 codes are distinct (v01 through v24), so each second-collection unit contributes exactly one `b` entry.", "observed_value": ["v12","v13","v14","v15","v16","v17","v18","v19","v20","v21","v22","v23","v24","v01","v02","v03","v04","v05","v06","v07","v08","v09","v10","v11"], "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "u07,v12,t01,1.0,2.0"}]}, {"description": "The row-independent procedure ttest_ind was applied to all rows; the reported df of 46 (24+24-2) matches one entry per distinct unit on each side.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.ttest_ind(left, right)"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "df=np.float64(46.0)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The measurement values show a suggestive structure (consecutive rows with near-duplicate values such as 1.0/1.5 and 2.0/2.25), which could hint at clustered generation; however, value similarity alone does not demonstrate repeated entry of the same identified unit, and the k1/k2 identifiers are all distinct.", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "u08,v13,t02,1.5,2.25"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to falsify the no-issue verdict by scanning all 24 rows for any repeated k1 or k2 code and by testing whether the near-duplicate numeric values in adjacent rows could constitute repeated unit entries. No identifier repeats; the task defines unit identity by k1/k2, and under that definition every entry corresponds to a distinct unit, so value similarity cannot establish the issue class from the visible files.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"},
{"case_id": "case:7232c367dbb013d06cde", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "All twelve k1 codes are distinct (u01 through u12) and all twelve k2 codes are distinct (odd-index v codes plus v01,v03,v05), so no unit contributes more than one measurement on either side.", "observed_value": {"k1": ["u01","u02","u03","u04","u05","u06","u07","u08","u09","u10","u11","u12"], "k2": ["v07","v09","v11","v13","v15","v17","v19","v21","v23","v01","v03","v05"]}, "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0"}]}, {"description": "The procedure applied is the Mann-Whitney U test, a row-independent two-sample procedure, receiving exactly one entry per distinct unit per side.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.mannwhitneyu(left, right)"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "MannwhitneyuResult(statistic=np.float64(60.5)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The only route to the issue class would be repeated k1 or k2 codes; a full scan of both key columns across all 12 rows found none, so the repeated-unit precondition is absent.", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "k1,k2,tag,a,b"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict by checking every k1 and k2 value for duplicates and by verifying that the workflow does not replicate rows before analysis (it reads the CSV once and passes each column list directly to mannwhitneyu). Both checks confirmed one entry per distinct unit; no repeated-unit entry into the row-independent procedure is demonstrable.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"},
{"case_id": "case:7edf0bd613868960a22c", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "All twelve k1 codes and all twelve k2 codes are distinct, so each source unit on each side contributes exactly one measurement; no unit enters the procedure more than once.", "observed_value": {"k1": ["u01","u02","u03","u04","u05","u06","u07","u08","u09","u10","u11","u12"], "k2": ["v07","v09","v11","v13","v15","v17","v19","v21","v23","v01","v03","v05"]}, "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0"}]}, {"description": "The reported df of 11 confirms 12 row-pairs were consumed, matching one entry per distinct unit; there is no repetition of any unit's data.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "df=np.int64(11)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The workflow applies a paired t-test (ttest_rel) even though the task states the row pairing is a storage convention with no matching relationship. This is a serious methodological concern, but it is the inverse pattern (imposing dependence that does not exist), not repeated entry of the same unit into a row-independent procedure, and ttest_rel is not a row-independent procedure in the sense of this issue class.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.ttest_rel(left, right)"}, {"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "The row pairing is a storage convention only; there is no matching, pairing, block, or other relationship between the `k1` item and the `k2` item in that row."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict two ways: (1) scanning for any duplicated k1 or k2 code, finding none; (2) testing whether the unjustified use of ttest_rel could itself qualify as this issue class. It cannot: the in-scope class requires the same unit to enter a row-independent procedure repeatedly, whereas here each unit appears once and the defect is an unauthorized pairing assumption, which is out of scope for this review.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"},
{"case_id": "case:afa5a8a02fb0e223e9c7", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "In this case only, each of the twelve first-collection source items identified by k1 (u01 through u12) appears in exactly two staged rows, contributing two `a` measurements each; the workflow feeds all 24 `a` entries into scipy's ttest_ind, a procedure that treats every row entry as an independent observation, and the report's df of 46 confirms all repeated per-unit entries were counted as independent. The reported p-value of 0.3953 therefore rests on an inflated effective sample size for the `a` side.", "root_cause": "The workflow passes the raw per-row `a` column directly into a row-independent two-sample t-test without aggregating or otherwise accounting for the fact that the task defines k1 as identifying the measured source item and each k1 code recurs twice, so repeated measurements of the same authorized unit are entered as if they were distinct independent units.", "issue_class": "issue-class:repeated-authorized-independent-unit-entry-into-row-independent-procedure", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task defines k1 as identifying the first-collection source item measured by column `a`, making k1 the unit identifier for the left sample.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "`k1` identifies a first-collection source item measured by column `a`"}]}, {"description": "Each k1 code appears exactly twice: for example u01 appears on the first two data rows with two different `a` values (1.0 and 1.5); the same doubling holds for u02 through u12 across the 24 rows.", "observed_value": {"u01": 2, "u02": 2, "u03": 2, "u04": 2, "u05": 2, "u06": 2, "u07": 2, "u08": 2, "u09": 2, "u10": 2, "u11": 2, "u12": 2}, "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "u01,v08,t02,1.5,2.25"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 24, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "u12,v06,t24,12.5,12.25"}]}, {"description": "The workflow builds the left sample from every row's `a` value with no per-unit aggregation and applies ttest_ind, which assumes each entry is an independent observation.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 6, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "left = [float(row[\"a\"]) for row in staged]"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.ttest_ind(left, right)"}]}, {"description": "The report's df of 46 (24+24-2) shows all 24 per-row entries per side were counted as independent observations, i.e., the twelve k1 units were each counted twice on the `a` side.", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "df=np.float64(46.0)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The k2 codes are all distinct (v01 through v24), so the `b` side has no repeated units; the issue is demonstrated only on the `a` side. This limits the scope of the defect but does not negate it, since ttest_ind's independence assumption is violated by either sample.", "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "u01,v07,t01,1.0,2.0"}]}, {"description": "One could argue the task's instruction to apply the procedure to 'the complete staged row sequence' authorizes using all rows; however, that instruction governs which rows are in scope, and it does not change the fact that the same identified unit's measurements were entered repeatedly into a procedure whose validity rests on one independent entry per unit.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Apply the named procedure to the complete staged row sequence."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to defeat the demonstrated-issue verdict three ways: (1) checking whether the repeated k1 codes might be typographical coincidence — they are not, since the task explicitly states k1 identifies the measured source item and every one of the twelve codes recurs exactly twice in a systematic layout; (2) checking whether the workflow deduplicates or aggregates per unit before testing — it does not, it maps every row directly into the sample lists; (3) checking whether the report might reflect a deduplicated run — the df of 46 proves all 24 entries per side were used. All three falsification routes failed, so the verdict stands.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"},
{"case_id": "case:bbc57eefb5fe9183e72d", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task explicitly states that k1 and k2 are opaque codes and that the task does not establish whether either code identifies a source item, so a repeated k1 code cannot, from the visible files, be shown to be a repeated entry of the same source unit.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Treat `k1` and `k2` as opaque codes; `tag` is an opaque annotation. This task does not establish whether either code identifies a source item within either collection."}]}, {"description": "The workflow applies ttest_ind to all rows and the report's df of 22 matches the 12 rows per side; nothing in the workflow or report itself establishes that any single source unit was entered more than once.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 8, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "result = st.ttest_ind(left, right)"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "df=np.float64(22.0)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Each k1 code (u01 through u06) appears exactly twice — for example u01 on the first two data rows — which is the pattern that would demonstrate the issue if k1 were established as a unit identifier for the `a` measurements. This is the strongest evidence against my verdict, but the task affirmatively withholds that identification, so the repetition of an opaque code does not demonstrate repeated entry of the same source unit.", "observed_value": {"u01": 2, "u02": 2, "u03": 2, "u04": 2, "u05": 2, "u06": 2}, "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 2, "end_line": 3, "quoted_text": "u01,v11,t02,2.0,4.0"}, {"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 13, "quoted_text": "u06,v02,t12,12.0,12.0"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I attempted to overturn the no-issue verdict by treating the doubled k1 codes as evidence of repeated units entering ttest_ind. The attempt fails on the task's own terms: the task instructs that the codes are opaque and expressly states it does not establish that either code identifies a source item, and the instruction not to guess unstated intentions bars me from inferring that identity. Without a visible-file basis linking repeated codes to repeated source units, the issue class is not demonstrated; the suspicious pattern remains a concern outside what these files can establish.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "medium"}
]}